  "typical_application": "Sequencers, LED chasers, and frequency division stepping through ten decoded outputs in order.",
  "gotchas": [
    "decoded outputs are NOT in pin-number order: Q0=3, Q1=2, Q2=4, Q3=7, Q4=10, Q5=1, Q6=5, Q7=6, Q8=9, Q9=11",
    "RESET (MR, pin 15) is active HIGH; tie LOW for normal counting, do not float",
    "advances on the rising edge only while CLOCK INHIBIT (pin 13) is LOW; clock on a falling edge by feeding pin 13 and holding pin 14 HIGH",
    "CARRY OUT (pin 12) is distinct from Q9 (pin 11); easy to confuse",
    "only one output is HIGH at a time; do not wire-OR expecting overlap"
  ],
